<title>LITHUANIA: Lithuanian three-month T-bill yield dips.</title>
<headline>Lithuanian three-month T-bill yield dips.</headline>
<dateline>VILNIUS 1997-03-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average yield on Lithuanian three-month paper dipped at an auction on Monday to 9.56 percent from 10.01 percent last week, the central bank said.</p>
<p>All amounts are in millions of litas.</p>
<p> MATURITY   AV YIELD   LAST TIME   MIN/MAX   ISSUE  BID  SOLD</p>
<p> 92-day	 9.56	 10.0     8.80/10.0   50   67.21  50</p>
<p>Settlement date for the auction is March 6, and the bills mature on June 6.</p>
<p>The next auction is on March 4 when 50 million litas ($12.5 million) of 182-day paper will be offered.</p>
<p>-- Riga Newsroom, +371 721 5240 ($ = 3.997 Lithuanian Litas)</p>
</text>
